TASK-2 ENVIRONMENT

Task-2 is a compositional two-stage transform service.

It preserves the same 64-cell ring and C/S directional streams but changes the request computation.

Each request carries:

- immutable four-bit input x0;
- stage-A truth-table program PA;
- stage-B truth-table program PB;
- stream direction C or S;
- creation epoch;
- deterministic request id.

The generic four-bit truth-table interpreter remains:

index = a | (b << 1) | (c << 2) | (d << 3)
output = (program >> index) & 1

STAGE A

yA = PA(x0)

STAGE B

Construct x1 by replacing the first bit of x0 with yA while preserving the remaining three original bits.

yB = PB(x1)

The verified task answer is yB.

Thus every successful request requires two causally ordered processing operations rather than one.

REQUEST LIFECYCLE

RAW
-> SENSED
-> PROCESSED_A
-> PROCESSED_B
-> ROUTING
-> AT_EGRESS
-> VERIFIED
-> DONE

A verification failure enters REPAIR_PENDING and must recompute both stages from immutable provenance before independent re-verification.

No request may skip either processing stage.

TASK-2 PROGRAM DERIVATION

The LU-2G implementation must freeze before primary Task-2 programs exist.

Let the implementation freeze commit be LU2GF1.

For each fresh primary replicate, derive stage-A and stage-B balanced, non-constant, non-affine 16-bit truth tables deterministically from:

LU2G-TASK2|LU2GF1|replicate|stream|stage|counter

Programs must be distinct within each replicate unless deterministic duplicate resolution is required.

No difficulty filtering.
No rejection based on performance.
No program replacement after manifest binding.

LOAD NORMALIZATION

Task-1 used six requests per epoch with one PROCESS operation per request.

Task-2 requires two PROCESS operations per request.

Therefore Task-2 uses exactly three requests per epoch.

This is fixed before primary execution to preserve approximately the same nominal PROCESS-operation demand rather than doubling computational load and confounding task transfer with a pure load shock.

The five 32-epoch demand phases remain structurally analogous:

Phase 0 balanced;
Phase 1 C-heavy;
Phase 2 S-heavy;
Phase 3 distributed lesion;
Phase 4 anchor relocation.

Three-request phase schedules must be deterministic and frozen in the manifest.

No phase identifier is exposed to OBS-V1.

OBSERVATION BOUNDARY

Learned U inference receives exactly OBS-V1.

No Task-2 program contents.
No program id.
No stage id.
No request id.
No phase id.
No absolute position.
No global queue length.
No evaluator correctness.
No future information.
No teacher-derived feature supplied to the model.

The exact teacher U distribution may be used only outside the learned model to construct the preregistered alpha=.25 probability blend.

